{
  // Type-checks the test files, which tsconfig.app.json excludes.
  //
  // Relaxations vs the app config, with the reason each is off and what turning
  // it back on costs. Measured 2026-07-27 against this tree, one flag at a time,
  // over the 157 test files this config puts in scope:
  //   noUncheckedIndexedAccess  off  +136 errors -- `rows[0].name` in a fixture
  //                                                 the test just built is not a
  //                                                 real nullability risk
  //   noUnusedLocals            off   +16 errors -- fixture scaffolding
  //   noUnusedParameters        off    +1 error  -- a stub signature
  //   all three on                   +153 errors
  // The config is at 0 errors as it stands. `strict` itself stays ON: this
  // config exists so a test asserting against a stale interface fails, and that
  // does not depend on the index/unused flags. Production code keeps all three.
  //
  // These are re-measured numbers. The first version of this comment recorded
  // 156/25/3 and "253 strict", which was 69 (the residual that sized the
  // clean-up) plus the three deltas -- a sum, not a measurement, and these
  // errors do not add. Turn a flag on and count before acting on any of them.
  //
  // `exclude: []` is load-bearing. `extends` inherits the base `exclude`, so
  // without this line tsconfig.app.json's `src/**/*.test.ts(x)` exclusions win
  // over the `include` below and this config checks nothing at all.
  //
  // `types` must be listed explicitly because naming it at all replaces the
  // default "every @types package" behaviour: vitest/globals for describe/it,
  // node for `global` in setupTests.ts. src/vite-env.d.ts is included for
  // `import.meta.env`, which production modules pulled in by tests rely on.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.app.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "types": ["vitest/globals", "node"],
    "noEmit": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": false,
    "noUnusedLocals": false,
    "noUnusedParameters": false
  },
  "include": [
    "src/**/*.test.ts",
    "src/**/*.test.tsx",
    "src/test-utils/**/*",
    "src/setupTests.ts",
    "src/vite-env.d.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": []
}
